{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan approved and implementation handoff recorded, 2026-08-25.\n\nCREATED EVIDENCE-FIRST BUGS\n- `shimmery-customary-dorking` / 831f-326d-be85-437a — `--ref`-targeted completion may mix pinned code with live-checkout inputs. The ticket requires a divergent A/B real-path experiment and classification of every code read before any fix; intentional live comparisons may reject/retry but verdict evidence must come from the supplied `--ref`. A falsifying experiment closes the bug without a refactor.\n- `lineny-barathea-ladybug` / 7dea-2f00-db57-4a96 — parallel completion-cache writers may collide on the shared per-criterion `.tmp` path. The ticket requires barrier-controlled thread and cross-process experiments, including suppressed-exception/final-payload evidence, before any unique-temp-path change. A falsifying experiment closes the bug unchanged.\nBoth bugs are linked `discovered_from` this research ticket.\n\nAPPROVED IMPLEMENTATION STORY\n- `sedate-villainous-teledu` / b03c-f8d4-ef82-4618 — use a lazy pinned ticket view and atomically publish completion-close artifacts. The story pins independent `code_oid` and `tickets_oid`, records typed exact/negative/hierarchy/link/global read receipts, validates relevant deltas, keeps expensive work outside the lock, and makes PASS `COMPLETION_VERDICT` + closing `STATUS` + completion `SIGNATURE` one rollback-safe local commit before ordinary fast-forward publication. It explicitly forbids force ref updates/pushes.\n- Concrete file impact: 14 source/test/doc paths. Verification: focused lazy-view and atomic-close suites, compatibility suites, then lint/typecheck/test in CI. No local suite was run because the operator requested CI-only testing on this resource-limited host.\n- Signed plan review: PASS, 0 blocking / 5 advisory, verified at code SHA 8b8fa7c0064557c6746afc948e3cb0a8786c83a1, material 131e841d6c8bd7cf, Bedrock Claude Sonnet 4.6. Total 216,867.7 ms (3m36.9s), deterministic 5,796.9 ms, LLM 188,974.7 ms, 29 model requests.\n- Advisory implementation guardrails retained without invalidating the approved signed plan: assert bounded object reads/no full materialization; make individual AC oracles explicit; bound repeated push-CAS retries and surface termination; evict stale OID-keyed derived indexes; reclaim per-run temporaries on abort/restart/crash.\n\nNo production code, repository docs, tests, or agent guidance changed during this research/handoff."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787680037492310001,"uuid":"9b6efc74-d708-491d-aea6-824699e164bc"}